    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **70 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` feature for the create-owner flow (checkpoint cp58). `riskFlag` is a server-derived, read-time boolean on the owner response \u2014 the same shape as the existing `capacityWarning` / `bulkSignupWarning` fields \u2014 that is `true` when **any** of these three signals hold, otherwise `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 the stored `possibleDuplicate` soft-match flag (set by `AssignPossibleDuplicate`).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2014 a new check added to `OwnerEmail` (which owns the disposable blocklist). Since exact blocklisted domains are already rejected with 400 at create time, \"adjacent\" catches the ones that *do* get stored: same registrable name under a different suffix (e.g. `mailinator.org`) or a subdomain of a blocked domain (e.g. `smtp.mailinator.com`).\n3. **City over its soft capacity** \u2014 reuses `CapacityWarning` (the 40-owner soft band short of the hard limit of 50), keeping the threshold defined in one place and keeping `riskFlag` consistent with `capacityWarning`.\n\nChanges:\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` schema to `OwnerDto` (read-only boolean), which generates the setter.\n- `OwnerEmail.java` \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(...)` plus a `secondLevelLabel(...)` helper.\n- `RiskFlag.java` (new) \u2014 the OR of the three signals, mirroring `CapacityWarning`/`BulkSignup`.\n- `RespondWithOwner.java` (GET) and `RespondWithOwnerCreated.java` (POST) \u2014 set `riskFlag` on the DTO, matching where the other derived warnings are set.\n\nThe cp58 test and all 70 existing tests pass.",
